WEBVTT

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:09.250
Imagine knowing exactly what you want to say…

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:11.260
and having no way to say it out loud.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:16.130
After a total laryngectomy, the voice box is gone.

00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:20.500
Many people can still shape words with their lips, but there's

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:21.990
no sound behind them.

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:23.820
The words are still there.

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:24.950
The voice isn't.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:30.160
So we asked a simple question.

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:34.150
What if the words you can still mouth silently became another

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:35.000
way to speak?

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:35.850
That's TACIT.

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:38.600
It lives quietly in the notch of your Mac.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:45.330
Start it once.

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:49.570
TACIT reads your lips through the camera, never your microphone,

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:53.740
and a visual speech recognition model running on your Mac turns

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:55.730
silent articulation into text.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:57.440
No sound at all.

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:58.090
Just lips.

00:00:58.090 --> 00:00:59.650
And the words come back.

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:13.820
Recognition isn't perfect, so nothing is spoken until you decide.

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:16.530
Here, "doing" came back as "going".

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:17.380
You see it.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:18.230
You fix it.

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:26.400
[TACIT voice] “How are you doing?”

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:31.020
When the words are right, one tap on Speak sends exactly those

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:35.230
words, in the voice you chose, into your call's microphone.

00:01:35.230 --> 00:01:37.510
And Stop is always one tap away.

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:40.680
But a conversation is more than sentences.

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:41.480
It's timing.

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:45.520
Hold my turn keeps your place, so nobody talks over you while

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:46.310
you compose.

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:49.090
[TACIT voice] “One moment, I'm responding.”

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:53.760
Saved phrases let you react in a second, in words that sound like you.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:57.660
And for practised phrases, an optional real-time mode speaks

00:01:57.660 --> 00:02:01.180
without review, only after you accept a clear warning.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:06.450
My Voice lets you choose how you sound, and preview it privately first.

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:10.970
Help Me Respond turns context you paste in into wording you can edit.

00:02:10.970 --> 00:02:14.830
It never listens to your meeting, and it never rewrites the

00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:16.340
words TACIT recognized.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:21.100
Under the hood: the camera, on-device lip tracking, visual

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:25.330
speech recognition, your review, voice synthesis, and a virtual

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:28.020
microphone that any calling app can use.

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:29.590
We're early.

00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:33.280
Accuracy varies, and TACIT hasn't been tested with people who've

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:34.270
lost their voice.

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:37.840
But we think everyone deserves more ways to be heard, on their

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:38.420
own terms.

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:40.110
TACIT.

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:41.050
Your words.

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:41.990
Your voice.

00:02:41.990 --> 00:02:43.180
Beyond speech.
